Imagine that tomorrow an artificial intelligence produces correct solutions to one thousand major scientific problems.

This would unquestionably be extraordinary.

It would not mean humanity has solved one thousand problems.

It would mean humanity possesses:

1000\ \text{candidate solutions}

sitting at the beginning of:

1000\ \text{implementation pipelines}.

Unfortunately, implementation pipelines contain irritating objects.

Factories.

People.

Machines.

Materials.

Hospitals.

Testing laboratories.

Regulators.

Construction crews.

Supply chains.

Failure analysis.

Maintenance.

Capital.

