7. Intelligence Does Not Abolish Causality

This principle deserves formal status.

\boxed{\text{Intelligence does not abolish causality}}

A chemical reaction still requires time.

A biological organism still develops through time.

Concrete still cures.

Metal still has to be machined.

Clinical outcomes still have to be observed.

Factories still occupy physical space.

A ship carrying equipment from one continent to another remains stubbornly larger than an API call.

AI may optimise these processes enormously.

It cannot simply announce:

PROCESS COMPLETE

and intimidate the atoms into agreement.

