8. The Medical Island

Medicine provides perhaps the cleanest illustration.

Imagine an AI discovers tomorrow how to cure every major cancer.

For the purpose of this thought experiment, assume the science is completely correct.

This would be one of the greatest discoveries in human history.

Humanity would still have an enormous problem:

producing the fucking cures.

Each therapy may require:

* synthesis;
* biological manufacturing;
* specialist equipment;
* quality control;
* toxicology;
* dosing studies;
* trials;
* regulatory approval;
* diagnostic infrastructure;
* trained clinicians;
* distribution;
* refrigeration;
* monitoring;
* and manufacturing capacity measured in actual physical units rather than tokens.

Some therapies might reach patients quickly.

Replacing an entire global treatment system could take decades.

The discovery is instantaneous.

The civilisation is not.

