10. Standard Operating Civilisation

The first successful end-to-end mission would create something considerably more valuable than another capability announcement.

It would produce procedures.

For example:

AI scientific output validation protocol

Laboratory handoff specification

Human expert review requirements

Physical testing escalation process

Regulatory evidence package

Manufacturing transfer protocol

Deployment monitoring framework

Suddenly the second problem becomes easier.

Not necessarily because the AI became smarter.

Because civilisation finally built the fucking plumbing.

This is how mature industries operate.

Aircraft are not built by announcing:

“We have become very good at aerodynamics.”

They exist because thousands of interfaces have been standardised.

Materials.

Fasteners.

Inspection.

Manufacturing.

Testing.

Documentation.

Maintenance.

Certification.

Training.

The miracle is not merely that humans understand lift.

The miracle is that we built an entire system capable of repeatedly converting that understanding into several hundred tonnes of aluminium crossing an ocean without killing everyone.

AI presently has plenty of lift.

What it lacks is Boeing.

Preferably Boeing from one of the better decades.

