11. The Skills Paradox Returns

There is an additional complication.

The same society expecting AI to transform every industry is simultaneously weakening many of the human expertise pipelines required to implement the transformation.

Beginner work is automated.

Training budgets disappear.

Employers demand experienced hires.

Experts retire.

Tacit knowledge vanishes.

Then AI generates increasingly sophisticated instructions requiring humans capable of recognising whether they are bullshit.

Excellent.

We therefore approach:

\text{AI output complexity}\uparrow

while

\text{human verification capacity}\downarrow.

This represents what the Institute classifies as:

Advanced Instruction / Reduced Interpreter Syndrome

or:

AIRIS

The system produces increasingly advanced maps while gradually firing the people who know what mountains look like.

