12. The Strawberry Safety Case

The current state of AI reliability deserves particular attention.

A system may perform advanced mathematical manipulation in one interaction and then fail an elementary task in another.

This variability is amusing when the question is:

How many letters R are in strawberry?

It becomes somewhat less charming when the instruction is:

Please autonomously perform vascular surgery.

The necessary transition is enormous.

Today’s occasional failure mode:

confidently incorrect answer

Future autonomous surgical failure mode:

patient has unfortunately become two patients

The standards are therefore different.

A useful assistant can be wrong occasionally.

A fully autonomous physical system operating on human beings must achieve reliability orders of magnitude beyond:

usually pretty good.

