The metaphor can now be formalised.

Each demonstrated AI capability is an island.

Some islands are enormous.

Some contain extraordinary resources.

Some may genuinely change civilisation.

But islands become economically transformative only when connected.

Ports.

Bridges.

Shipping routes.

Standards.

Maps.

Infrastructure.

Institutions.

People.

The current AI economy resembles an age of exploration in which sailors discover a new continent every Thursday and nobody remembers where the previous one was.

