16. The One-Finished-Thing Test

This paper therefore proposes a simple benchmark.

Not:

How many domains can the model demonstrate capability in?

But:

\boxed{\text{How many important problems has the complete AI-human system actually finished?}}

Finished means:

* validated;
* deployed;
* usable;
* reproducible;
* maintainable;
* materially improving the intended outcome.

The benchmark is deliberately cruel.

A paper does not score.

A prototype does not score.

A benchmark does not score.

A viral demonstration does not score.

The scoreboard moves when reality changes.

