18. The Omnipotence Error

The mythical omnipotent AI is therefore conceptually confused.

An intelligence can know enormous amounts.

It can discover enormous amounts.

It may eventually exceed human cognitive capability across almost every measurable domain.

It still inhabits a universe.

The universe contains:

finite energy;

finite matter;

finite space;

finite manufacturing capacity;

finite experimental throughput;

and the profoundly annoying requirement that Tuesday must occur after Monday.

There is no intelligence level at which causality becomes optional.

